5 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431038 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431045 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431045 1077 "selection" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431045 1078 #edb/ref 17592186431038 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431045 1079 #uuid "c7e0a66d-4420-5ec9-9e88-13a5cdd58112" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431046 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431014 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431046 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431015 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431046 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431022 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431046 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431030 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431046 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431040 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431046 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431046 1077 "selection" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431046 1078 #edb/ref 17592186431022 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431046 1079 #uuid "d3715f35-6d8a-57c2-a089-fd1bb9bddf47" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431047 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431013 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431047 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431025 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431047 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431033 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431047 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431035 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431047 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431041 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431047 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431047 1077 "selection" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431047 1078 #edb/ref 17592186431025 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431047 1079 #uuid "fd054105-4a4d-5e12-a937-81dcca4212b8" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431048 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431046 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431048 1069 "q-126574" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431048 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431048 1071 "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nI. $F(x,y)=⟨y{e}^{x},\\,x-{e}^{x}⟩$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=⟨2y,\\,x⟩$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{2x}{3}+1⟩$" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431048 1072 #uuid "1d67db6a-7337-599e-8ecc-26284642ae3b" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431048 1074 "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1-{e}^{x},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-2{e}^{x}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{3}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{2}{3},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431049 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431042 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431049 1069 "q-126760" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431049 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431049 1071 "![](images/a9/a95b161dab89fe1245724921ef4ee36112d7a4062e7e171411e4ffe61253b91f.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$ for $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}].$ \nThe area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}\\boxed{}\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ Determine the missing part of the equation.\n\n*Hint: Note that $C$ is negatively oriented.*" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431049 1072 #uuid "2177a684-6e86-5255-ac01-04a426569ee5" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431049 1074 "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since the path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431050 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431047 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431050 1069 "q-126575" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431050 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431050 1071 "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nI. $F(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3},\\,{x}^{3}+1⟩$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{2}+\\sqrt{2}x,\\,\\frac{3x}{2}⟩$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=⟨x,\\,x⟩$" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431050 1072 #uuid "2c0dea55-217c-592d-9a6c-d305c8e67729" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431050 1074 "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3{x}^{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{3}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431051 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431044 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431051 1069 "q-126727" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431051 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431051 1071 "![](images/b5/b51e252935f7077f3285258845d8d1e4957b83894037f968ee306910aa88bad6.png)\n\nUse Green's theorem to find the area of the region enclosed by the curve \n$C$ parametrized as $r(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j$ \nfor $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].$" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431051 1072 #uuid "819104c2-11eb-5b49-9398-d7d5879660f9" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431051 1074 "First, let $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$\n\nOur simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y=-{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate our line integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{∮}_{C}y\\,dx & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{u}^{3}{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}({1}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431052 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431043 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431052 1069 "q-126859" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431052 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431052 1071 "![](images/9e/9ebabcf1e3c3c3d2f4850d425657e7314c0135c81a432bfbbc8ae31ee39cb85d.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2},$ where \n\n- ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)={t}^{5}\\,i-2{t}^{4}\\,j$ for $t\\in [-1,1],$ and\n\n- ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=-t\\,i-2\\,j$ for $t\\in [-1,1].$\n\nUse Green's theorem to find the area of the region." 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431052 1072 #uuid "bd34f4a5-5a97-5165-88b5-594ad30569e0" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431052 1074 "First, let $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ \n\nOur simple, piecewise-smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and   \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since our path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y=-{∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivatives of ${r}_{1}(t)$ and ${r}_{2}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\, & {r}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}\\,i-8{t}^{3}\\,j \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\, & {r}_{2}^{′}(t)=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}}x\\,dy \\\\  & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}x\\,dy-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}x\\,dy \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{5}\\cdot (-8{t}^{3})\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-t)\\cdot 0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{8}\\,\\text{d}t+0 \\\\  & =8[\\frac{{t}^{9}}{9}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431053 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431045 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431053 1069 "q-126761" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431053 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431053 1071 "![](images/10/10f4094edb09afc7908bd0cd3df089387c8f5b762ea5ef86da152d1c9d08b5e4.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t)=⟨{sin}^{5}⁡t,\\,{cos}^{5}⁡t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$ \nThe area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\boxed{}\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ Determine the missing part of the equation.\n\n*Hint: Note that $C$ is negatively oriented.*" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431053 1072 #uuid "d1f25e51-cfc7-5f63-98bf-d803b12546e2" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true] [17592186431053 1074 "Our simple, piecewise-smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since the path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨5{sin}^{4}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-5{cos}^{4}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-{sin}^{5}⁡t)\\cdot (-5{cos}^{4}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }5{sin}^{6}⁡t{cos}^{4}⁡t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534653 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-031791c1-0f2f-546c-82e8-999c8554dc97" 17592186431012 "answer-0de6da70-c426-566d-b3d0-dce7471f5600" 17592186431013 "answer-1f503e12-e11c-54c7-8ba7-5830ef6f73bd" 17592186431014 "answer-20a55ace-f5e1-5a5a-91ce-2c0b7d1404a1" 17592186431015 "answer-2b151d74-5c74-545d-8b07-dea1d8453657" 17592186431016 "answer-30625b21-0638-5df6-8e7f-5ecca67ca674" 17592186431017 "answer-31a713ed-2a9a-58c6-bfc8-e17df3a2f279" 17592186431018 "answer-32eb8a32-3dbf-536c-8383-dfb162184c29" 17592186431019 "answer-419ff17a-c941-551d-ad1c-89eccf44a609" 17592186431020 "answer-46ee80ff-c5ae-55ec-a96c-b506acfb7915" 17592186431021 "answer-4798dafc-c73d-5ec4-b12f-da6f6620e4dd" 17592186431022 "answer-4addbefd-201e-5755-8641-7e27605c3311" 17592186431023 "answer-4b345484-1be0-5dbb-8ec3-b21aa5962d50" 17592186431024 "answer-576c0bfb-effc-5ce5-827d-af6530c65e4e" 17592186431025 "answer-7643c9ff-155d-5092-a735-8716263f25b6" 17592186431026 "answer-7a937f5d-4690-55ac-bcf9-5662d89ca2a9" 17592186431027 "answer-7bf73cdb-b201-56ec-9e65-ae9499b1e5c5" 17592186431028 "answer-88f605ff-e892-57f0-8a1b-c76ad9f5a91e" 17592186431029 "answer-8a583e9f-a399-590a-ac83-6aef2ccb73c6" 17592186431030 "answer-a3a3e7c7-ac4d-53f3-be35-8650eb6afd4d" 17592186431031 "answer-a4547936-89a5-5eb1-a5c2-aca7ffed8e29" 17592186431032 "answer-a5d96a71-7dc4-568f-af4e-fef495f9c448" 17592186431033 "answer-b4200cd7-229f-5b2c-80d8-6fbc6195eb39" 17592186431034 "answer-cd786957-3ffe-55c0-a40e-e21f738990d5" 17592186431035 "answer-dd351131-c322-54cb-